Subject: [PATCH] Resume the last tab instead of the startup NTP home surface

Chromium replaces the last active tab with a fresh New Tab Page "home
surface" when Chrome is launched from the launcher after the return-time
threshold (4 hours by default), both on cold start and when an existing
instance is resumed. The previous tabs are restored behind it, so reopening
the browser after a close or a reboot reads as "a new tab on startup"
instead of continuing where the user left off.

Keep the last active tab on screen. The NTP itself is still reachable; it
just stops being the startup surface.

---
diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ChromeTabbedActivity.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ChromeTabbedActivity.java
--- a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ChromeTabbedActivity.java
+++ b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ChromeTabbedActivity.java
@@ -5818,17 +5818,14 @@
     public ChromeNextTabPolicySupplier getNextTabPolicySupplier() {
         return (ChromeNextTabPolicySupplier) mNextTabPolicySupplier;
     }
 
     /** Returns whether to show a NTP as the home surface at startup on tablet in regular mode. */
     private boolean shouldShowNtpHomeSurfaceOnStartup() {
-        if (mTabModelSelector.isIncognitoSelected()) return false;
-
-        assert mInactivityTrackerSupplier.get() != null;
-        return ReturnToChromeUtil.shouldShowNtpAsHomeSurfaceAtStartup(
-                getIntent(),
-                getSavedInstanceState(),
-                getPersistentInstanceState(),
-                mInactivityTrackerSupplier.get());
+        // Resume the last active tab. Chromium otherwise swaps it for a fresh
+        // NTP home surface once Chrome has been away for the return-time
+        // threshold (4 hours by default), on cold start and on warm resume,
+        // which reads as "a new tab" instead of continuing the last session.
+        return false;
     }
 
